.TH CARAVAN 1 "April 2026" "caravan 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
caravan \- safe staged data migration tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B caravan
.RI [ --log-level " LEVEL ] " COMMAND " [OPTIONS]
.PP
.B caravan
.B status
.RI [ --state " PATH ] " [ --output " {human|json} ]"
.PP
.B caravan
.B resume
.RI [ --state " PATH ] " [ --recover-failed ] " [ --inspect-failed ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBcaravan\fR performs conservative staged migration with explicit safety gates.
It is designed for Windows staging (Storage Spaces to NTFS) and Linux migration
(NTFS to Btrfs).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B staging
Run transfer in staging mode.
Requires \fB--source\fR, \fB--dest\fR, and \fB--batch-size\fR.
.TP
.B migrate
Run transfer in migrate mode.
Supports snapshot cadence with \fB--snapshot-every\fR.
.TP
.B status
Show migration state summary.
.TP
.B resume
Continue from an existing state file.
.SH SAFETY GATES
.IP "1." 3
Verification gate: failed verification blocks destructive actions.
.IP "2." 3
Deletion gate: verified batches still require approval before delete.
.IP "3." 3
Conflict gate: default policy (\fBskip-file\fR) avoids overwriting conflicts.
.IP "4." 3
Capacity gate: copy is blocked when free space is less than or equal to planned batch size.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --interactive
Enable interactive approval for destructive operations.
.TP
.B --conflict-policy " {skip-file|skip-batch}"
Conflict behavior for transfer copy.
Default: \fBskip-file\fR.
.TP
.B --skip-conflicts
Legacy compatibility flag mapped to \fBskip-file\fR behavior.
.TP
.B --copy-buffer-size " SIZE"
Buffered-copy chunk size (default: 16 MiB).
.TP
.B --buffered-copy-threshold " SIZE"
Files at or above this size use buffered copy (default: 8 MiB).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Staging:
.PP
.EX
caravan staging --source D:\\Data --dest E:\\staging --batch-size 100GiB --interactive
.EE
.PP
Migration:
.PP
.EX
caravan migrate --source /mnt/staging/Data --dest /mnt/data/@media --batch-size 100GiB --snapshot-every 1 --interactive
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B .caravan/
State directory containing migration state and registry metadata.
